---
title: Stuart meets Satoshi - first contact on the p2p channel
---

%% Before a key rotation, Stuart and Satoshi exchange DIDs and verify each other.
%% Both peers do the same steps. The diagram shows one direction: Satoshi verifies Stuart.

sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Stu as Stuart (DID controller)
    participant BTC as Bitcoin blockchain ⛓
    participant CAS as CAS / IPFS 📦 (optional)
    actor Sat as Satoshi (channel peer)
    participant Res as Satoshi's resolver

    rect rgba(128, 128, 128, 0.08)
    Note over Stu: 1. Create the DID (offline, no cost)
    alt k1 DID
        Stu->>Stu: New secp256k1 key → did:btcr2:k1…<br/>Initial DID Document: initialKey and 3 Singleton Beacons
    else x1 DID
        Stu->>Stu: Genesis Document (id did:btcr2:_, keys, beacons)<br/>→ SHA256(JCS(Genesis Document)) → did:btcr2:x1…
        opt CAS distribution (public)
            Stu->>CAS: Publish the Genesis Document
        end
    end
    end

    rect rgba(128, 128, 128, 0.08)
    Note over Stu,BTC: 2. Prepare for updates (one time)
    Stu->>BTC: Fund a Beacon Address:<br/>each Beacon Signal spends a UTXO of this address
    end

    rect rgba(128, 128, 128, 0.08)
    Note over Stu,Res: 3. First contact
    Stu->>Sat: Channel message signed with a key of the DID,<br/>did, Sidecar Data (Genesis Document if x1, all updates)
    Sat->>Res: resolve(did, { sidecar })
    alt x1 DID and no Genesis Document in the Sidecar Data
        Res->>CAS: Get the Genesis Document by genesis_bytes
        CAS-->>Res: Genesis Document (hash checked)
    end
    Res->>BTC: Find Beacon Signals of each Beacon Address
    BTC-->>Res: Beacon Signals (none for a new DID)
    Res-->>Sat: didDocument (version N) and didDocumentMetadata
    Sat->>Sat: Check: not deactivated, message key is in authentication.<br/>Verify the message. Store: Stuart's keys at version N.
    end

    Note over Stu,Sat: Next: key rotation with a Singleton, CAS, or SMT Beacon.
